'''Sartan Baliscans''' ([[Baliscano]] and {{Langx|es|sartano-baliscano}}) refers to [[Baliscans]] citizens of full or partial [[Sartan people|Sartan]] ancestry or persons born in the territories of the former [[Sartan Confederation]] who reside in [[Balisca]] and/or speak [[W:Castilian language|Sartan]]. This definition is controversial, as not all people in the former terrorities consider themselves Sartan. For that reason, the exact limits of what is "[[Sarta (historical region)|Sartan]]" today are disputed. 

Sartan Baliscans form the third-largest [[Illypnian Baliscans|Illypnian ancestry]] group in the confederation. Between 1857 and 1946, 500,000 Sartan people immigrated to Balisca, predominately to [[Bayara]] and [[Hesperia]]. Besides Illypnian immigration, Balisca has also received, as early as the 1840s, immigrants with Sarta background from other territories, notably [[Volisania]], [[Jacan]] and [[Breisland]], which has bolstered the community.

